# Character image uploads

## Goal
Use the existing private MinIO/S3 infrastructure to store one portrait image per character, expose it in Forge with upload/replace/remove controls, and persist the durable image object reference in the character JSON.

## Data flow
- Forge requests a character-scoped presigned PUT URL from a server action.
- The browser uploads the selected image directly to MinIO with `PUT`.
- Forge writes the returned durable object metadata into the Zustand character store.
- Existing autosave/manual save persists that metadata in the character JSON blob.
- On load, Forge requests a fresh presigned GET URL for the stored object key and uses it for preview.

## Scope
- Add optional character image metadata to `CharacterData`.
- Add defaults/hydration fallback for existing characters.
- Add server actions for presigned upload, preview URL generation, and object deletion.
- Add a Forge image upload/preview component in the Bio tab.
- Keep the bucket private and use signed GET URLs instead of public object URLs.
- Configure MinIO CORS for browser PUT/GET from the app origin.
